-- חוזר לבעלויות תשס"ז/5 — קיזוז שכר מעובדי הוראה בשל עיצומים/שביתות מלאות בשנת הלימודים תשס"ז (7.6.2007)
-- The further full-strike dates of the secondary teachers' organisation
-- after 11.3.2007, by district and grade; salary is deducted from every
-- teacher who took part, for the days and hours of the strike.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT common

§ `קיזוז שכר בשל עיצומים/שביתות מלאות תשס"ז`

-- akn:hc_1/p1 akn:hc_1/p2 akn:hc_1/p3 akn:hc_1/p4 akn:hc_1/p5 akn:hc_1/p6 akn:hc_1/p7 akn:hc_1/p8 akn:hc_1/p9 The letterhead, title, date, addressee and subject line; no rule.

-- akn:hc_1/p10 akn:hc_1/p11 akn:hc_1/p12 The background: following circular תשס"ז/3 of 11.3.2007, the secondary teachers' organisation went on holding full strikes in several localities.

§§ `The further strike dates`

@desc One printed line of the strike dates: the day, where, which grades, and from what hour (0 for the whole day).
DECLARE `strike line` HAS
    `strike date`      IS A DATE
    `where`            IS A STRING
    `lowest grade`     IS A NUMBER  @desc 7 = ז'
    `highest grade`    IS A NUMBER  @desc 12 = יב', 14 = יד'
    `from hour`        IS A NUMBER  @desc the hour the strike began, 0 when it covered the whole day

-- The list as printed (¶16–38). Grades are numbered (ז' = 7 … יד' = 14);
-- "בכיתות ח'" on 14.5.2007 is grades 8 to 8.
@ref akn:hc_1/p15 akn:hc_1/p16 akn:hc_1/p17 akn:hc_1/p18 akn:hc_1/p19 akn:hc_1/p20 akn:hc_1/p21 akn:hc_1/p22 akn:hc_1/p23 akn:hc_1/p24 akn:hc_1/p25 akn:hc_1/p26 akn:hc_1/p27 akn:hc_1/p28 akn:hc_1/p29 akn:hc_1/p30 akn:hc_1/p31 akn:hc_1/p32 akn:hc_1/p33 akn:hc_1/p34 akn:hc_1/p35 akn:hc_1/p36 akn:hc_1/p37 akn:hc_1/p38
`the further strike lines` MEANS
    LIST `strike line` (Date 22 2 2007) "all districts (omitted by mistake from circular 3)" 7 12 0,
         `strike line` (Date 12 3 2007) "Tel Aviv district" 7 14 0,
         `strike line` (Date 13 3 2007) "Jerusalem district, Jerusalem administration, and Ulpanat Tzvia in the south" 7 14 0,
         `strike line` (Date 14 3 2007) "Haifa district and Ulpanat Tzvia in the south" 7 14 0,
         `strike line` (Date 15 3 2007) "Northern and Southern districts" 7 14 0,
         `strike line` (Date 11 4 2007) "all districts" 7 12 0,
         `strike line` (Date 12 4 2007) "all districts" 7 12 0,
         `strike line` (Date 17 4 2007) "all districts" 7 12 0,
         `strike line` (Date 19 4 2007) "all districts" 7 12 0,
         `strike line` (Date 20 4 2007) "ORT and Amal networks, the whole country" 7 12 0,
         `strike line` (Date 26 4 2007) "Northern and Southern districts (except ORT and Amal)" 7 12 0,
         `strike line` (Date 29 4 2007) "Jerusalem district and Jerusalem administration (except ORT and Amal)" 7 12 0,
         `strike line` (Date 30 4 2007) "Tel Aviv and Haifa districts (except ORT and Amal)" 7 12 0,
         `strike line` (Date 1 5 2007) "Central district (except ORT and Amal)" 7 12 0,
         `strike line` (Date 2 5 2007) "all districts" 7 9 0,
         `strike line` (Date 7 5 2007) "Southern district (except the Gaza-envelope localities)" 7 12 0,
         `strike line` (Date 8 5 2007) "Northern district" 7 12 0,
         `strike line` (Date 9 5 2007) "Tel Aviv district" 7 12 0,
         `strike line` (Date 13 5 2007) "Haifa district" 7 12 11,
         `strike line` (Date 14 5 2007) "the whole country, 8th-grade classes" 8 8 0,
         `strike line` (Date 15 5 2007) "Tel Aviv district" 7 12 11,
         `strike line` (Date 17 5 2007) "Jerusalem district and Jerusalem administration" 7 12 11,
         `strike line` (Date 20 5 2007) "Southern district" 7 12 11

§§ `The deduction`

@desc One lesson hour of a teacher's fixed timetable.
DECLARE `timetable hour` HAS
    `lesson date`              IS A DATE
    `lesson starts at`         IS A NUMBER  @desc the hour of day the lesson begins (e.g. 11)
    `grade taught`             IS A NUMBER
    `school is covered`        IS A BOOLEAN @desc the school lies where the strike line says (district, network); an input
    `the teacher struck it`    IS A BOOLEAN @desc the teacher took part in the strike for this hour

GIVEN h IS A `timetable hour`, l IS A `strike line`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the line covers` h l IF
        h's `lesson date` EQUALS l's `strike date`
    AND h's `school is covered`
    AND h's `grade taught` AT LEAST l's `lowest grade`
    AND h's `grade taught` AT MOST l's `highest grade`
    AND h's `lesson starts at` AT LEAST l's `from hour`

-- ¶13–14: by the State's decision no salary is paid for taking part in a
-- strike; it is deducted from every teacher who did, for the days and hours
-- in which they took part.
@ref akn:hc_1/p13 akn:hc_1/p14
GIVEN h IS A `timetable hour`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the hour is deducted` h IF
        h's `the teacher struck it`
    AND any (GIVEN l YIELD `the line covers` h l) `the further strike lines`

-- ¶39: the owning body deducts by the teacher's fixed timetable at the school.
@ref akn:hc_1/p39
GIVEN `value of one hour` IS A NUMBER
      hours IS A LIST OF `timetable hour`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `salary to deduct` `value of one hour` hours IS
    count (filter `the hour is deducted` hours) TIMES `value of one hour`

DECLARE `strike action` IS ONE OF
    `deduct the salary` HAS `amount deducted` IS A NUMBER
    `offset in the standing payments` HAS `hours offset` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `value of one hour` IS A NUMBER
      hours IS A LIST OF `timetable hour`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `strike action`
DECIDE `the owning body deducts the strike salary` `value of one hour` hours IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MUST  `deduct the salary` amount
          PROVIDED amount AT LEAST `salary to deduct` `value of one hour` hours

-- ¶40–41: the Ministry offsets the owning bodies through the current
-- standing payments (מת"מ), by the budgeted hours of the striking
-- institutions and the dates and localities of the strike. A description of
-- what the Ministry does; the hours are its figure, an input.
@ref akn:hc_1/p40 akn:hc_1/p41
GIVEN `budgeted hours of the striking institutions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `strike action`
DECIDE `the Ministry offsets the strike` `budgeted hours of the striking institutions` IS
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
    MUST  `offset in the standing payments` h
          PROVIDED h EQUALS `budgeted hours of the striking institutions`

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off and signature; no rule.

-- Examples (hour value 100 is a placeholder). Three hours on 13.5.2007 in
-- Haifa: the strike began at 11:00, so only the 11:00 and 12:00 hours count.
`three Haifa hours on 13 May` MEANS
    LIST `timetable hour` (Date 13 5 2007) 9 10 TRUE TRUE,
         `timetable hour` (Date 13 5 2007) 11 10 TRUE TRUE,
         `timetable hour` (Date 13 5 2007) 12 10 TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT `salary to deduct` 100 `three Haifa hours on 13 May` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT count `the further strike lines` EQUALS 23

-- A 10th-grade hour on 2.5.2007 is not covered: that day's strike was ז'–ט'.
`a 10th-grade hour on 2 May` MEANS
    `timetable hour` WITH
        `lesson date`           IS Date 2 5 2007
        `lesson starts at`      IS 8
        `grade taught`          IS 10
        `school is covered`     IS TRUE
        `the teacher struck it` IS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the hour is deducted` `a 10th-grade hour on 2 May`

#TRACE `the owning body deducts the strike salary` 100 `three Haifa hours on 13 May` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `deduct the salary` 200 AT 1
